===== README.md [Once] =====
# demo-workers

Camunda 8 job workers generated by `bpmnkit worker gen --lang rust`.

```sh
cargo run     # start the workers (REST; CAMUNDA_REST_ADDRESS, default http://localhost:8080)
cargo test
```

## Job types

- `agent-loop` → `src/handlers/agent_loop.rs`

## Ownership

- `src/gen/` and `src/handlers/mod.rs` are overwritten by `bpmnkit worker gen` (`DO NOT EDIT`). Check drift in CI with `--check`.
- Everything else (handlers, tests, `main.rs`, `Cargo.toml`) is written once and never overwritten.
- Delivery is at-least-once: handlers must be idempotent.
===== src/gen/agent_loop.rs [Generated] =====
// @generated by bpmnkit <version> — sha256:db88f295d58bfdcfa40c5a5e08246be515faf3841ef75be8dfa6ef0562de3679 — DO NOT EDIT
use bpmnkit_worker::{ActivatedJob, Complete, Handler, JobError, WorkerConfig};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
pub const JOB_TYPE: &str = "agent-loop";
/// Variables fetched for the job: the declared inputs. Empty means all (none declared).
pub const FETCH_VARIABLES: &[&str] = &[];
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, Deserialize)]
pub struct AgentLoopInput {}
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, Serialize)]
pub struct AgentLoopOutput {}
/// Implement this in `src/handlers/agent_loop.rs`. Delivery is at-least-once: be idempotent.
pub trait AgentLoopHandler: Send + Sync + 'static {
    fn handle(
        &self,
        input: AgentLoopInput,
        job: &ActivatedJob,
    ) -> impl std::future::Future<Output = Result<AgentLoopOutput, JobError>> + Send;
}
/// The worker settings of this job type; chain more builder calls to tune them.
pub fn config() -> WorkerConfig {
    let config = WorkerConfig::new(JOB_TYPE);
    if FETCH_VARIABLES.is_empty() {
        config
    } else {
        config.fetch_variables(FETCH_VARIABLES.iter().copied())
    }
}
/// Wraps a handler as a worker [`Handler`]: variables in, variables out, errors mapped.
pub struct Adapter<H>(pub H);
impl<H: AgentLoopHandler> Handler for Adapter<H> {
    async fn handle(&self, job: ActivatedJob) -> Result<Complete, JobError> {
        let input: AgentLoopInput = serde_json::from_value(
                serde_json::Value::Object(job.variables.clone()),
            )
            .map_err(|e| JobError::fail(
                format!("invalid variables for job type {JOB_TYPE}: {e}"),
            ))?;
        let output = self.0.handle(input, &job).await?;
        Complete::output(&output)
    }
}
